uministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 76 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.900 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no indica malas prácticas. Puede deberse a circunstancias como presupuestos cerrados o necesidades específicas. No hay datos que confirman abusos o errores.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos al límite abarcan necesidades similares. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre reflejan patrones recurrentes.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 155 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 33.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.7 to 5.8. December accounts for 6% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 11% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 16. Contract [1], for 14,900 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts were just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices might be lower than expected, or budgets might be fixed. Other reasons could explain the amounts without any improper action.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of the December contracts to see if they follow a pattern. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they are related or if they cover different needs. Look at the specific contract [1] to understand what was purchased and why it was just under the limit.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["Jpm6WGPzaRc36J9Lctlsuw%3D%3D","%2BMK56UOZQ%2FyTylGzYmBF9Q%3D%3D","vMrRrHLtSxhq1DdmE7eaXg